From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+alilinux@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:09:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mips: nommu headers (pgtable_no, uaccess_no, generic mm
 hooks): P2

New headers (m68k/microblaze patterns):

- pgtable_no.h: trivial page tables; 4level-fixup folds pud_* onto
  pgd_*, pmd_t exists only to satisfy generic declarations; swapper_pg_dir,
  VMALLOC_{START,END}, ZERO_PAGE=BUG, update_mmu_cache no-op.
- uaccess_no.h: includes asm-generic/uaccess.h (userland runs in kernel mode,
  'user' pointers are kernel pointers: access_ok() is always true, copies
  are memcpy).  exception_table_entry::nextinsn is renamed 'fixup' to match
  the generic struct (arch/mips/mm/extable.c, traps.c).

Gated behind CONFIG_MMU (nommu branches added):

- asm/pgtable.h -> pgtable_no.h
- asm/uaccess.h -> uaccess_no.h
- asm/mmu.h -> asm-generic/mmu.h (end_brk for sys_brk in mm/nommu.c)
- asm/mmu_context.h -> asm-generic/mmu_context.h (no ASID bookkeeping)
- asm/tlbflush.h -> asm-generic/tlbflush.h
- asm/pgalloc.h: body compiled only under MMU (asm-generic/tlb.h keeps
  compiling, nothing uses mmu_gather under nommu: memory.o is MMU-only)

Also:

- uapi/asm/mman.h: define MAP_UNINITIALIZED (mm/nommu.c needs it; MIPS
  has its own uapi mman.h, not the asm-generic one).
- kernel/asm-offsets.c: page-table DEFINEs (PGD/PMD/PTRS_PER_*, orders)
  moved under CONFIG_MMU; MM_PGD stays (mm_struct::pgd is unconditional).

Status (ali_c3503d_defconfig, MMU=n): kernel/ fs/ mm/ net/ lib/ crypto/
block/ ipc/ security/ all build warning-free.  Regression (malta, MMU=y):
fork.o memory.o exec.o read_write.o signal.o traps.o mm/init.o fault.o
build clean.  Tree still does not link under nommu -- P3 gates the
arch/mips TLB files out of the build (docs/nommu_mipsel_implementation.md).
